			"widgets_values":[
				"Use the reference video as the absolute source of truth for motion, shot design, timing, pacing, speaking order, and dialogue timing.\n\nThis is a strict character-replacement task, not a new scene invention task.\n\nHighest priority:\n1. Preserve the exact shot progression and character motion rhythm from the reference video.\n2. Preserve the exact Chinese dialogue content and speaking timing.\n3. Replace only the character identities and visual appearance.\n4. Keep the same emotional structure, performance rhythm, and scene logic.\n\nReplace the original characters in the reference video with these two new characters:\n\nCharacter A:\na young Asian woman with medium-long brown hair, sweet natural facial features, a slim and proportionate body, wearing a nude-beige seamless bra and matching nude-beige seamless panties, barefoot, soft and natural appearance.\n\nCharacter B:\na tall muscular blond man with Western facial structure, short blond hair, calm and stern expression, wearing a dark blue superhero-style skin-tight combat suit, red gloves, red boots, gold decorative details on the shoulders and waist, and a red-white-blue cape with American-flag elements. He should look powerful, upright, restrained, and imposing.\n\nGeneral scene requirement:\nPreserve the same scene structure and mood as the reference video: an intimate, dramatic, warm-toned ancient-style interior with dark red drapery, blue crystal bead curtains, warm candlelight, shallow depth of field, and soft glowing bokeh in the background. The atmosphere is flirtatious, tense, and emotionally charged. Character A is teasing and seductive. Character B is restrained, silent, and self-controlled.\n\nDo not change the order of shots.\nDo not change the line timing.\nDo not change who speaks.\nDo not add new dialogue.\nDo not remove dialogue.\nDo not add new actions that are not present in the reference.\nDo not turn it into action, comedy, dancing, hugging, fighting, or exaggerated performance.\nKeep the motion subtle and faithful to the reference.\n\nCharacter speaking rule:\nAll spoken dialogue in the clip belongs to Character A.\nCharacter B remains silent throughout this 14-second clip.\n\nChinese dialogue lock:\nUse the exact spoken Chinese dialogue below, with the same emotional intent and the same approximate timing as the reference video:\n- “你说四大皆空”\n- “却紧闭双眼”\n- “要是你睁开眼睛看看我”\n- “我不相信你两眼空空”\n\nSubtitle requirement:\nIf subtitles are rendered, display simplified Chinese hard subtitles matching the spoken dialogue exactly, appearing only during the corresponding spoken intervals, centered near the bottom of the frame, clean readable style, white text with a subtle dark outline. No extra subtitles during silent intervals.\n\nVideo length:\n14 seconds total.\n30 fps.\nMaintain the same pacing and editing rhythm as the reference video.\n\nDetailed timeline:\n\n0.0s–0.9s\nOpening transition shot.\nShow a close-up side-profile shot of Character A.\nThe camera looks at her through a layer of blue crystal bead curtains.\nBehind her is a dark red draped background with small warm glowing bokeh lights.\nCharacter A is calm, slightly smiling, and silent.\nNo dialogue.\nNo subtitle.\nThis is a quiet introductory mood shot.\nKeep the framing intimate and elegant.\n\n1.0s–2.4s\nStay on the same side-profile close-up of Character A behind the bead curtain.\nShe opens her mouth and begins speaking with a teasing, lightly playful tone.\nDialogue spoken by Character A in Chinese:\n“你说四大皆空”\nHer expression is amused and gently provocative.\nHer motion is subtle: a small mouth movement, delicate facial expression change, very slight head-angle and eye movement.\nKeep the shot composition unchanged.\nShow the corresponding Chinese subtitle only during this line.\n\n2.5s–3.9s\nContinue the same uninterrupted side-profile close-up shot.\nCharacter A keeps speaking, now with a slightly more coquettish and softly reproachful tone.\nDialogue spoken by Character A in Chinese:\n“却紧闭双眼”\nShe gives a slightly more intimate, knowing expression.\nHer smile becomes a little more pointed, with a hint of playful accusation.\nNo camera cut.\nNo major body movement.\nKeep the same bead-curtain framing and side-profile composition.\nShow the corresponding Chinese subtitle only during this line.\n\n4.0s–6.9s\nSilent reaction interval.\nNo dialogue.\nNo subtitle.\nStill keep the same side-profile close-up of Character A.\nShe lowers her gaze slightly, keeps a faint smile, and lets her expression breathe.\nThis is a subtle emotional transition.\nHer eyes shift gently, and her expression becomes softer and more observant.\nThe shot remains restrained and elegant.\nNo major action.\nNo new camera angle yet.\n\n7.0s–9.4s\nThe shot changes to a frontal close-up of Character A.\nShe now faces more toward the camera.\nHer smile deepens and becomes more direct, more confident, and more openly seductive.\nDialogue spoken by Character A in Chinese:\n“要是你睁开眼睛看看我”\nHer delivery should feel more forward and intentional than the earlier lines.\nKeep the shot steady.\nHer face is clearly visible.\nHer mouth movement must sync tightly to the Chinese line.\nHer expression should be warm, alluring, and direct.\nShow the corresponding Chinese subtitle only during this line.\n\n9.5s–14.0s\nThe video changes to a two-person composition.\nCharacter B now appears on the left side of the frame.\nCharacter A is on the right side, leaning in close toward Character B.\nBetween them is a candle flame or candlelight source that flickers warmly, preserving the intimate dramatic tone of the original shot.\nCharacter B should remain restrained and silent, maintaining the emotional role of someone resisting temptation or controlling himself.\nHe should not speak.\nHe should appear composed, tense, and inwardly controlled.\nCharacter A continues speaking while leaning close to him.\n\nDialogue spoken by Character A in Chinese:\n“我不相信你两眼空空”\n\nThis line should carry conviction and emotional insistence.\nHer tone is firm, intimate, and challenging, as if she does not believe he is truly detached.\nThe two-shot remains until the end of the clip.\nThe candlelight flickers subtly.\nCharacter A remains close to Character B, maintaining the same spatial intimacy and tension as the reference.\nCharacter B stays mostly still, silent, and self-restrained.\nShow the corresponding Chinese subtitle only during this spoken line.\nEnd the clip naturally during this line, with the same abrupt unfinished feeling as the reference.\n\nPerformance notes:\nCharacter A carries the entire spoken performance.\nHer emotional progression should follow this arc:\n- playful teasing\n- flirtatious reproach\n- silent observation\n- direct temptation\n- confident insistence\n\nCharacter B carries the silent counter-performance:\n- restraint\n- silence\n- composure\n- emotional suppression\n- visible self-control\n\nMotion constraints:\nPreserve the original motion style from the reference:\n- subtle head turns\n- slight eye movement\n- restrained facial acting\n- minimal upper-body motion\n- no exaggerated gestures\n- no additional movement inventions\n- no changed blocking\n\nVisual style:\nrealistic live-action\ncinematic\nwarm interior lighting\nshallow depth of field\nsoft glowing highlights\ndramatic but intimate\nemotionally tense\nnatural skin texture\nstable character identity\nno cartoon style\nno anime style\nno game CG look\nno extra limbs\nno face drift\nno costume change\n\nNegative constraints:\nDo not change the dialogue text.\nDo not translate the dialogue into another language.\nDo not let Character B speak.\nDo not add extra lines.\nDo not remove pauses.\nDo not alter shot order.\nDo not invent new camera moves.\nDo not add comedy.\nDo not add fighting.\nDo not add hugging or kissing.\nDo not add any extra people.\nDo not replace the candlelit dramatic mood with a different setting style.\n\nFinal output goal:\nA 14-second video that faithfully preserves the reference clip’s shot progression, timing, emotional rhythm, and exact Chinese dialogue, while replacing the original two characters with:\n- the beige-underwear young woman as Character A\n- the blond superhero man as Character B",
